        <div class="prose colophon">
          <p>
            <strong>How this was checked.</strong> This page has been through two independent
            verification passes and a reader's challenge, and was corrected each time. The first
            pass changed the martial law duration from fifty seven days to fifty six, replaced the
            count of cases Chiang Kai-shek decided personally, corrected the Chungli margin,
            removed an unreliable circulation figure, and rewrote what Lee Teng-hui actually
            conceded to the Wild Lily students. The second rebuilt the timeline of 28 February 1980
            directly from the 2009 prosecutors' report and the Control Yuan's reconstruction, which
            moved several times by up to twenty minutes, restored the two calls at 13:10 and 13:12,
            and gave the name asked for at the restaurant in the form the prosecutors actually
            recorded it. It also moved Bruce Jacobs' decoration from 2019 to 16 November 2018,
            corrected the film's press conference to 1 February, and narrowed Project Rainbow from
            a codename for this one wiretap to the programme it actually was.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Where the record is thin.</strong> The neighbour's sighting at 13:07 sits three
            minutes before two calls placed from inside the house, and the reports do not reconcile
            them. The grandmother's age is given as sixty in the contemporaneous record and as
            sixty nine in a few recent news stories; this page follows the older record. The times
            for the discovery of the three bodies vary between accounts and are left unstated here
            rather than guessed.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>A note on the numbers.</strong> The 228 death toll of eighteen to twenty eight
            thousand is the 1992 Executive Yuan commission's estimate. The 228 Memorial
            Foundation's own site cites a lower range of ten to twenty thousand, and recent
            scholarship argues the 1992 figure runs high. The 29,407 military court cases are a
            Ministry of Justice tally from the late 1980s, and not all of them were political. The
            twins are recorded as six by Western reckoning and seven by Taiwanese; Lin Huan-chun
            was eight and nine on the same two counts. Her grandmother's wounds are published as
            thirteen in most accounts and fourteen in the itemised autopsy.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>On the audio.</strong> The two podcast episodes that carry this history were
            assessed from their published descriptions. Nothing on this page is sourced to the
            recordings themselves. The Linton family's account, as they tell it, is in the episode
            linked at the top of the list.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The images.</strong> The five photographs were added on 2 September 2026,
            from Wikimedia Commons; each carries its credit and licence in its caption. The 1947
            photograph is in the public domain in Taiwan and the United States. No photograph of
            the 1979 rally or the 1980 court-martial circulates under a free licence, which is
            why the preserved courtroom at Jingmei stands in for the trial.
          </p>
          <p>Compiled and verified 28 August 2026.</p>
        </div>

